    "remaining_open_items": [
      "Magnetizing and leakage inductance, core loss, interwinding capacitance and detailed safety insulation qualification remain unestablished.",
      "Former simulation blocker resolved for the explicitly bound reference (2026-10-08): Do not claim safe galvanic isolation or a complete response from assumed 1 H / 5 mH / 100 pF. Resolution: Closed by a DC-only winding binding that uses none of the assumed LP/LLK/CIW values: primary 1-3 = 44 ohm nominal and secondary 4-6 = 58 ohm nominal, as printed on the archived Triad TY-145P sheet (publish date 2026-02-23). The centre taps (pins 2, 5) are required_isolated because the half-winding split is not published. The model has no inter-winding element; limitations state this is not an isolation claim (1500 V is 'Dielectric Strength Pri to Sec to Core', a test value) and that no AC transfer or frequency response is simulated (op only). Pin functions now come from the part's own sheet, replacing the DEFAULT-ASSUMPTION map.",
      "Magnetising and leakage inductance, interwinding capacitance and core loss for any AC binding",
      "Half-winding DCR split (centre taps)",
      "Insulation/isolation qualification (never claimed)"
